    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Kyle Tucker** (75.29) and **Andy Pages** (70.97), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Pfaadt. **Kyle Tucker** holds our highest daily efficiency score, elevated by a strong SP skill matchup and a solid park factor. Meanwhile, **Andy Pages** provides a dual threat; beyond his solid base projection, he is a primary target for stolen base opportunities due to the opponent's slow delivery, a critical component given our organizational emphasis on speed. **Jacob Wilson** also earns a prime spot with a score of 69.79, buoyed by the wind conditions and a park shift that heavily favors his profile against Bennett. While we are tracking the \"Lineup Pending\" status for many of our stars, these three represent our most reliable paths to points across the 5x5 categories.\n\nManaging the bench requires balancing raw output against the scarcity of stolen bases and tough matchups. **Sam Antonacci** (46.73) was our closest exclusion; he put up a respectable score, but the combination of facing an elite arm in Gavin Williams and the superior efficiency of our active starters kept him on the pine. We are exercising caution with **Gunnar Henderson** (60.75), who faces the formidable deGrom. Despite the high-difficulty matchup, his elite ability to contribute across all categories keeps him in the lineup, though his potential for stolen bases is suppressed by a difficult hold-percentage environment. Finally, we remain in a holding pattern regarding the health of **Jordan Westburg**, whose absence from the active roster continues to limit our flexibility at the infield corners. Owners should monitor the official lineup releases for **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**, as any late-breaking shifts in the batting order could necessitate immediate recalibration of our expected efficiency.",
